Emitted Rime tables are a separate data product. Each lemma carries
source and license metadata in the SQLite store and in the emitted
NOTICE fragments. Do not treat this Apache-2.0 grant as a license
for third-party lexicon dumps.

Typical upstream licenses encountered during ingest (not bundled
here unless a fixture is a short original sample):

- Table of General Standard Chinese Characters (PRC) — official character list
- Unicode Unihan Database — Unicode License
- CC-CEDICT — Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike
- THUOCL — MIT
- Tencent AI Lab Chinese embedding vocabulary — CC BY 3.0
  (pinned coverage includes the ModelScope light high-frequency subset
  from lili666/text2vec-word2vec-tencent-chinese and the first 1,000,000
  source-order lines of the d200 v0.2.0 key list mirrored at pinned
  Hugging Face revision 26b432a69cca98e291a76b6e8e8890f3527b67b5.
  The mirror declares no separate license. ModelScope card Apache-2.0 is
  packaging only.)
- Official Rime luna_pinyin / essay / rime-emoji — LGPL-3.0
- Wikimedia dumps — CC BY-SA

Share-alike sources (CC-CEDICT, Wikipedia titles) must not be mixed
into a proprietary table without a recorded legal decision. Track them
in lemma_sources and in dist/rime/NOTICE.

This factory must not ingest rime-ice, rime-wanxiang recipe trees, or
commercial IME cell dictionaries. See CLEANROOM.md.
